--- resolvent identity (exact, new) ---
8T_S = 24I - 8 Gamma_S - B^T C B with C = 3I + M - J/2 (B = 14x44 letter incidence, M = mates).  If 3 is not an
eigenvalue of Gamma_S:  nu(T_S) = nullity(D),  D = B (3I - Gamma_S)^{-1} B^T - (3I - M - J/3)  (14 x 14);  D u_r = 0
automatically for u_r = 4e_r + e_r' - 1 (r = 0..3, exact star counts);  Conway (nu = 14) <=> D = 0.
Checked mod two large primes on 200 c=1 sides with 3 not in spec(Gamma_S): nu = 14 - rank D every time.
